---
description: Depot Insecure Packages
globs: *.nix
---
# Depot Insecure Packages

Rules for handling insecure packages in the depot repository with nix.

<rule>
name: insecure_packages
description: Standards for handling insecure package allowances
filters:
  - type: file_path
    pattern: "third_party/nixpkgs/default\\.nix$"
  - type: file_path
    pattern: ".*\\.nix$"
actions:
  - type: reject
    conditions:
      - pattern: "nixpkgs\\.config\\.permittedInsecurePackages"
        message: "Do not set permittedInsecurePackages at the module level. Add to //third_party/nixpkgs/default.nix instead"
  - type: suggest
    message: |
      Follow these conventions when allowing insecure packages:

      1. Add insecure package allowances to the global config in //third_party/nixpkgs/default.nix:
         ```nix
         config = {
           permittedInsecurePackages = [
             "package-name-version" # Required by service-name
           ];
         };
         ```

      2. Always include a comment explaining which service requires the package

      3. Do not set permittedInsecurePackages in:
         - Individual NixOS modules
         - Service configurations
         - Machine configurations

      4. If a service requires an insecure package, document it in the module's
         description or README.md

examples:
  - input: |
      # Bad: Setting at module level
      nixpkgs.config.permittedInsecurePackages = [ "package-1.2.3" ];

      # Good: Added to third_party/nixpkgs/default.nix
      permittedInsecurePackages = [
        "package-1.2.3" # Required by service-name
      ];
    output: "Correctly configured insecure package allowance"

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: 1.0
</rule>
